{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261116T081612Z_dev-04_flat_5e40", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "In the fixed-r comparison for the 4b on-shell cascade, the AMS-02 antiproton limits approach or intersect the GCE-preferred regions at the smaller ratios r = 0.2–0.4. At the larger ratios shown, the antiproton limits stay above the GCE-preferred regions, so they do not constrain them. The ratios shown run from r = 0.2 to 1.0, so this covers r ≈ 0.5–1.0. The text does not give separate numbers for each ratio; it only states this split.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "6.3"}]}, "turns": 11, "seconds": 29.911, "tool_calls": 10, "tool_result_chars": 588958, "input_tokens": 24, "output_tokens": 1107, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 259826, "cache_read_input_tokens": 1210011, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-16T08:16:42+00:00"}
